  "question_stem": "A particle $A$ moves in a straight line with constant speed $10 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$. Two seconds after $A$ passes a point $O$ on the line, a particle $B$ passes through $O$, moving along the line in the same direction as $A$. Particle $B$ has speed $16 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ at $O$ and has a constant deceleration of $2 \\text{ m s}^{-2}$.",
